WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.410
Seal a leafy shoot into
a tube full of water,

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:07.110
with one air bubble trapped
in a narrow side tube.

3
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.520
As the shoot takes up water,
the bubble creeps along a scale.

4
00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.170
Now switch on a fan beside the leaves.

5
00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:17.260
The bubble moves more than twice as fast.

6
00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:21.050
So why does a plant lose
water fastest on a warm,

7
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.670
dry, windy day, and
how can you measure it?

8
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.940
In this mission, you'll
test four outside factors,

9
00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.270
one at a time.

10
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:33.550
Then you'll turn a bubble's movement
into a rate of water uptake.

11
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.200
Your mission: explain why plants
lose water fastest on warm,

12
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:41.250
dry, windy days, and how to measure it.
